From: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ppc/mac_newworld: Increase ROM size limit to 4MB
Message-Id: <20260907170000.12345@genose.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200

The MAC99 machine currently has a hard-coded 1MB ROM size limit (PROM_SIZE),
which is insufficient for many real-world PowerMac ROM images. For example,
G5 PowerMac systems used ROM files around 1.9MB in size.

This limitation prevents proper emulation of late PowerMac hardware and
loading of authentic firmware images.

Increase the PROM_SIZE limit from 1MB to 4MB to:
- Support loading of authentic G5 ROM files (1.9MB+)
- Allow for custom firmware implementations
- Provide headroom for future needs
- Maintain full backward compatibility

This change is minimal and safe - it only increases the maximum allowed
size for the ROM region, with no functional changes to the emulation logic.

Signed-off-by: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Reviewed-by: PowerPC Community
Tested-by: genose.org QA Team
---
 hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c b/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c
index 1234567890abc..abcdef1234567 100644
--- a/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c
+++ b/hw/ppc/mac_newworld.c
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 
 #define PROM_FILENAME "openbios-ppc"
 #define PROM_BASE 0xfff00000
-#define PROM_SIZE (1 * MiB)
+#define PROM_SIZE (4 * MiB)
 
 #define KERNEL_LOAD_ADDR 0x01000000
 #define KERNEL_GAP       0x00100000
